  "articleBody": "Painting a foreclosed property can seem straightforward, but there are definitely some common traps you'll want to steer clear of. One of the biggest mistakes is under-scoping the repair work. Vacant homes can hide a lot of neglect, so what looks like a simple paint job can quickly become a much larger project if you haven't budgeted for extensive patching or repairs. Another common pitfall is skipping surface prep. Trust me, painting over a dirty or damaged surface is just asking for trouble – the paint won't adhere properly and you'll end up redoing it. It's also crucial to clarify exactly what's included in any estimate, especially when it comes to exclusions. Don't assume anything! Always verify that your painters have proper insurance and licensing; you don't want to be on the hook for accidents. And finally, don't overlook cleanup responsibilities or who's doing the final touch-ups. When you’re dealing with a property that needs a lot of TLC, getting a detailed quote that covers all these bases is key. For complex situations, it's always best to get a professional like HH Remodeling LLC to handle the project to ensure a smooth process and a quality finish.",
